## Why This Is Asked
This question probes the ability to design a scalable, lock-free IPC primitive that adapts to workload changes without pausing throughput-critical paths, while handling cross-NUMA coordination and safe memory reclamation.

## Key Concepts
- Lock-free resizing of a ring buffer without halting producers/consumers
- Cross-NUMA memory ordering and cache-coherence considerations
- Per-slot sequence counters to prevent ABA in a dynamic ring
- Epoch-based reclamation or hazard pointers for safe memory reuse
- Correctness under high contention and failure scenarios

## Code Example
```c
// Prototypes (illustrative)
typedef struct { uint64_t seq; void *data; } Slot;
typedef struct { Slot *slots; size_t cap; _Atomic void *ring_ptr; } Ring;

int enqueue(Ring *r, void *item);
int dequeue(Ring *r, void **out);
int resize_ring(Ring *r, size_t new_cap);
```

